   "description": "Winchester transloading from The Flat Rate Movers: ocean containers devanned and destuffed, counted, inspected and photographed with same-day written exception reporting, reworked (palletized, wrapped, labeled, sorted by destination, purchase order or SKU), restacked into 53ft domestic trailers, dispatched on I-81, I-66 and I-70 through the Virginia Inland Port and Port of Virginia chain, empty returned before per-diem, final mile by appointment. Container transloading jobs are quoted per job, agreed in writing before dispatch. Heavy assets in the 1,500–3,500 lb range move under SIR (Structural Integrity Relocation, L/360 floor deflection) as part of the same flat-rate job.",
